# LIQUID-01 — No nested loops over large collections

## Rationale

Nested iteration over products/variants is O(n·m) and is the most common cause of
slow or timeout-prone Liquid renders.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check liquid-performance <file>
```

Flags nested `{% for %}` blocks where either loop goes over a list that can be large
(products, variants, collections, search results, articles). Nested loops over
small fixed lists, such as `product.options_with_values` and their values, are fine.

## How to fix

Propose restructuring — precompute a map, use `where`/`map` filters, or limit
the inner set. Requires judgement; propose rather than auto-edit.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% for product in collection.products %}
  {% for variant in product.variants %}
    {{ variant.title }}
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% for product in collection.products limit: 24 %}
  {% assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}
  {{ selected_variant.title }}
{% endfor %}
```

Or drive the inner set from a scoped setting with an explicit `limit:`.
